-- The inbox reads a bounded number of rows on a large workspace. inbox_entries holds one row per inbox
-- conversation (one with a message or a note that is not merged away: exactly inbox-visible.ts), with the
-- inbox's sort key, the flags its views filter on, the ticket columns a filter or sort may name and its tags,
-- so a page walks an index in order and stops after its rows; hidden widget drafts are never read.
-- inbox_tallies counts those entries by workspace, group, assignee and flags; inbox_field_tallies also by
-- priority, status category, channel and status; inbox_tag_tallies by tag as well, so the views' totals, the
-- counts' standard numbers and a filter over those fields and a tag read a handful of rows. inbox_unread holds each member's unread entries, so the
-- unread view and count read one row per unread conversation. Every value is derived: the migration fills
-- them, and triggers on every table they derive from keep them current (imports write rows with plain
-- INSERTs, so write-path code could not). A restore rebuilds them from the restored rows.
-- sort_at: coalesce(created_at of the last message, updated_at), the inbox order. unresolved: resolved_at IS
-- NULL (the list); counts_open: COALESCE(resolved_at,0)=0 (the counts). ai: an AI row with an ai_id (the list
-- and the counts' human numbers); ai_profile: an AI row whose profile exists (the counts' AI number).
-- company_id: the contact's company in the workspace. contact_revision: the highest revision of a contact
-- message that was not imported (unread for a member when above the member's read revision). tags_key: the
-- ticket's tag ids in tag order, exactly the tags field of tickets/filters.ts (its own links in the workspace).
